Custom methods are one of the MOST important concepts in programming because they teach you how to:

* organize logic
* reuse code
* break problems into smaller parts
* write scalable applications

Methods are basically:

```text id="v5grdt"
named reusable instructions
```

Without methods, real applications would become gigantic unreadable messes.

---

# What a Method Really Is

Instead of rewriting code over and over:

```ruby id="ah3hvn"
p 5 * 2
p 10 * 2
p 20 * 2
```

you create reusable logic:

```ruby id="3g7fb8"
def number_doubled(number)
  return number * 2
end
```

Now you can reuse it forever:

```ruby id="4s4k20"
number_doubled(5)
number_doubled(10)
number_doubled(20)
```

This is HUGE in real engineering.

