# Real Engineering Skill You're Building

Methods teach:

* abstraction - means - hiding complicated details and exposing only what you need to use - Ex. word.upcase - You know: it makes letters uppercase But you do NOT need to know: how Ruby internally loops through characters, memory operations, low-level implementation
* organization
* modular thinking - means breaking a large problem/application into smaller organized pieces; instead of trying to build everything in one giant block of code.
* reusable logic
* scalability
* cleaner code

This is one of the biggest transitions from:

> “writing random scripts”

to:

> “building actual software”

